---
description: Java and Spring Boot conventions
globs: backend/**/*.java
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use Java 21 language features conservatively and clearly.
- Organize packages by domain, not controller/service/repository layers at the root.
- Use records for immutable API request and response models when appropriate.
- Validate all public API input at the boundary.
- Keep calculation logic in deterministic, side-effect-free domain services where possible.
- Use database migrations; do not use Hibernate schema creation.
- Return stable error codes and do not expose stack traces.
- Test calculation edge cases including empty samples, pushes, and combination props.
